{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ll use the pose-review skill to verify N4 and N5, sweep the full change, and validate the final draft with the dispatching engine. I’ll keep tests focused and let every command finish before ending the review.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short; git rev-parse HEAD; cat .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md; cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go; cat pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go; git diff 5c35b3a8..2bd80b69 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go; printenv POSE_REVIEW_CLI'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git status --short; git rev-parse HEAD; cat .agents/skills/pose-review/SKILL.md; cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go; cat pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go; git diff 5c35b3a8..2bd80b69 -- pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go; printenv POSE_REVIEW_CLI'","aggregated_output":"2bd80b6903c2a7b23c1f12a6be6bb283aa0ed8e7\n---\nname: pose-review\ndescription: Use for POSE pull-request or code review to verify controlled scope, preserved contracts, security and observability impact, risk-proportional validation, and escalation where applicable. Trigger keywords - review, code review, PR review, review opinion, ultrareview.\nwhen_to_use: Evaluating your own or another author's diff or PR under POSE. Use before commenting or approving to select rules, inspect validation evidence and prior decisions, and issue an actionable decision.\npose_schema_range: \"1-1\"\nclients: agents-skills, mcp, claude-code\ncapabilities: read\n---\n\n# Skill: pose-review\n\n## Required reading\n\n1. [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md).\n2. [`.pose/workflows/review.md`](../../../.pose/workflows/review.md).\n3. Applicable domain rules; security takes precedence in conflicts.\n\nResolve the selected task with `pose context --task <typed-or-qualified-artifact-ref> --json` before reviewing. Follow its canonical authority and stop on ambiguity, stale binding, unsupported metadata or `transfer-in-progress`. Use the qualified `xref:` scope for cross-project review; every cross-project write requires an explicit `POSE_PROJECT_ROOTS` binding and the current `context_revision` as `--expect-context`. Keep review evidence and its `POSE-Spec:` trailer in the authority repository.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Classify the change as feature, bugfix, refactor, documentation, or mixed.\n2. Run `pose assess tech-debt` during code review to ensure markers (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `stub`, `panic`) are covered by follow-ups or specs. Run `pose assess integrate` when touching inter-module contracts (Protobuf, Kafka, REST, MCP).\n3. Resolve `pose review bundle <scope> --explain` to inspect effective criteria, components and tool requirements.\n4. Run active required tools first, record why each recommended tool was used or skipped, and keep completion tools deferred until attestation.\n5. Select rules with `pose suggest review --path <affected-dir>` for every mapped component.\n6. Search `.pose/knowledge/` for prior module decisions, accepted risks, and pending follow-ups.\n7. Require deterministic `pose validate --strict` evidence matching delivery targets.\n8. Evaluate every required plan criterion, including cross-component boundaries. When the change adds or alters a governance gate, also answer: what is the cheapest way to satisfy this gate in form without producing its value, and what stops that? Point to the adversarial corpus case that proves it (`pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md`), or record the gap.\n9. Classify findings as critical, high, medium, or low with evidence and expected action.\n10. Run `pose recurrence-check --tolerant --window-days 14`; use recurrence escalation for a matching systemic signal.\n11. Create a handoff with `pose new-knowledge handoff <slug>` for accepted residual risk, monitoring, or deferred action.\n12. Seal the review subject with `pose review bundle <scope> --seal`.\n13. Prepare the mechanical half with `pose review auto-attest <bundle-id> --reviewer agent:<id>` — without `--apply` — and read `review_attestation.pending`: those are the criteria no registered check answers, and they are yours to answer. Then record the attestation with `pose review attest`, giving every judgment criterion a conclusion. `--apply` on auto-attest records only when nothing is pending; it refuses otherwise, and never answers a judgment criterion for you. An explicit attestation records `--criterion ID|passed|evidence` (or `not-applicable` with a rationale, or `finding` naming a recorded finding) and `--finding ID|severity|disposition|action|evidence[|owner|rationale|review-by]`; every finding needs a severity and an action, and an `accepted-risk` or `wont-fix` finding also needs an owner, a rationale and a review date. A `passed` criterion may cite only evidence the sealed bundle contains, of a class the criterion accepts. For a cross-project attestation, use the qualified `xref:` as the target argument to `pose review attest`, include `--expect-context <digest>` with `--apply`, and keep the explicit project binding; a bundle ID alone does not select an authority project.\n14. Run `pose review verify <scope>` and `pose review-check <scope>`; close only when both confirm a valid, approved attestation.\n15. Decide: approved, approved with reservations, changes requested, or rejected.\n16. When Contributor Mode is active, if review uncovers POSE linter false-positives, diagnostic frictions, or rule gaps, stage an improvement proposal with `pose contribute stage --type enhancement --title \"<summary>\"`.\n\n## Output requirements\n\n- Completed Rules applied during review section.\n- Bundle/plan digests and dispositions for required, recommended and deferred completion tools.\n- Severity-classified findings with expected actions.\n- Clear and actionable final decision.\n- Handoff when residual risk is accepted.\npackage cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\tposemodel \"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\"\n)\n\nconst reviewDraftCheckUsage = \"pose review draft-check [<bundle-id|run-id>] --draft <file> [--json]\"\n\n// cmdReviewDraftCheck reports the reasons a draft would be refused at\n// conclusion, writing nothing (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3).\nfunc cmdReviewDraftCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\tvar bundleID, draftPath string\n\tjsonOut := false\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n\t\tswitch args[i] {\n\t\tcase \"--json\":\n\t\t\tjsonOut = true\n\t\tcase \"--draft\":\n\t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) {\n\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: --draft needs a file\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\tdraftPath = args[i]\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(args[i], \"-\") || bundleID != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: unexpected argument \"+args[i]+\"\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tbundleID = args[i]\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif draftPath == \"\" {\n\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: name the draft with --draft\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\t}\n\traw, err := readReviewDraftInput(draftPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + err.Error())\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tstore := cliGovernedStore(root)\n\tvar reasons []string\n\tvar ctx *posemodel.ReviewDraftContext\n\tif contextPath := os.Getenv(posemodel.ReviewDraftContextEnv); contextPath != \"\" {\n\t\tread, err := posemodel.ReadReviewDraftContext(contextPath)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tctx = &read\n\t}\n\tswitch {\n\tcase bundleID == \"\" && ctx == nil:\n\t\treturn usageError(stderr, \"pose review draft-check: name the bundle; only a delegated review provides it\\nUsage: \"+reviewDraftCheckUsage)\n\tcase ctx != nil && (bundleID == \"\" || bundleID == ctx.Bundle.BundleID):\n\t\t// Inside a delegated review the sealed checkout holds no bundle: the\n\t\t// run's own bundle, named or not, is judged from the context the\n\t\t// dispatch wrote (review round 2, N5).\n\t\treasons = store.CheckReviewDraftIn(*ctx, string(raw), time.Now())\n\tdefault:\n\t\treasons, err = store.CheckReviewDraft(bundleID, string(raw), time.Now())\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tmsg := strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \")\n\t\t\tif ctx != nil {\n\t\t\t\tmsg += \"; this run's draft context holds bundle \" + ctx.Bundle.BundleID + \", which is checked when it is named or no reference is given\"\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + msg)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif jsonOut {\n\t\twriteJSON(stdout, map[string]any{\"ok\": len(reasons) == 0, \"reasons\": nonNilStrings(reasons)})\n\t} else if len(reasons) == 0 {\n\t\trender(stdout, stderr).ContractLine(\"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\")\n\t} else {\n\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n\t\tout.ContractLine(\"Draft check: the conclusion step would refuse this draft:\")\n\t\tfor _, r := range reasons {\n\t\t\tout.ContractLine(\"  - \" + r)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(reasons) > 0 {\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn 0\n}\n\nfunc nonNilStrings(v []string) []string {\n\tif v == nil {\n\t\treturn []string{}\n\t}\n\treturn v\n}\n\n// reviewDraftInputLimit bounds the draft read; a larger input is refused,\n// never judged by its prefix (review round 2, N4).\nconst reviewDraftInputLimit = 4 << 20\n\nfunc readReviewDraftInput(path string) ([]byte, error) {\n\tvar in io.Reader\n\tif path == \"-\" {\n\t\tin = os.Stdin\n\t} else {\n\t\tf, err := os.Open(path)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tdefer f.Close()\n\t\tin = f\n\t}\n\traw, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(in, reviewDraftInputLimit+1))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tif len(raw) > reviewDraftInputLimit {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the draft is larger than %d bytes; a run's final message that large is not checked by a prefix\", reviewDraftInputLimit)\n\t}\n\treturn raw, nil\n}\npackage pose\n\n// Draft check (spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal R3): the reasons the\n// conclusion step and the attestation preflight would refuse a reviewer's\n// draft, computed before the run ends and without writing anything. It\n// reuses the same parsers and content checks; only the run's own proof,\n// signature and identity, which do not exist yet, are left out.\n//\n// A sealed checkout holds the subject, not the bundle sealed over it nor the\n// run ledger, so the dispatch writes both to the run's private directory and\n// names it in ReviewDraftContextEnv.\n\nimport (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// ReviewDraftContextEnv names the file holding the bundle and round a draft\n// is checked against inside a delegated review.\nconst ReviewDraftContextEnv = \"POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT\"\n\n// ReviewCLIEnv names the executable of the engine that dispatched a review,\n// so the reviewer checks its draft with it and not with another installed\n// `pose` (review round 1).\nconst ReviewCLIEnv = \"POSE_REVIEW_CLI\"\n\nconst reviewDraftContextSchema = \"pose.review-draft-context/v1\"\n\n// ReviewDraftContext is what a draft is judged against: the sealed bundle and\n// the findings its round must account for.\ntype ReviewDraftContext struct {\n\tSchema string              `json:\"schema\"`\n\tBundle ReviewBundle        `json:\"bundle\"`\n\tRound  int                 `json:\"round\"`\n\tOpen   []ReviewOpenFinding `json:\"open,omitempty\"`\n}\n\n// ReviewDraftContextFor builds the context of bundle from the run ledger.\nfunc (s Store) ReviewDraftContextFor(bundle ReviewBundle) (ReviewDraftContext, error) {\n\tround, err := s.ReviewRoundOf(bundle)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ReviewDraftContext{}, err\n\t}\n\treturn ReviewDraftContext{Schema: reviewDraftContextSchema, Bundle: bundle, Round: round.Number, Open: round.Open}, nil\n}\n\n// writeReviewDraftContext writes ctx under dir and returns its path.\nfunc writeReviewDraftContext(dir string, ctx ReviewDraftContext) (string, error) {\n\traw, err := json.Marshal(ctx)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", err\n\t}\n\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, \"pose-review-draft-context.json\")\n\treturn path, os.WriteFile(path, raw, 0o600)\n}\n\n// ReadReviewDraftContext reads a context file a dispatch wrote.\nfunc ReadReviewDraftContext(path string) (ReviewDraftContext, error) {\n\tvar ctx ReviewDraftContext\n\traw, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn ctx, err\n\t}\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &ctx); err != nil {\n\t\treturn ctx, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: reading draft context %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\tif ctx.Schema != reviewDraftContextSchema || ctx.Bundle.BundleID == \"\" {\n\t\treturn ctx, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: %s is not a review draft context\", path)\n\t}\n\treturn ctx, nil\n}\n\n// CheckReviewDraft returns every reason a draft for ref would be refused at\n// conclusion, or nil when none applies. ref is a bundle id, or a run id whose\n// bundle is used.\nfunc (s Store) CheckReviewDraft(ref, output string, now time.Time) ([]string, error) {\n\tbundleID := ref\n\tif strings.HasPrefix(ref, \"rrn-\") {\n\t\trun, err := s.LoadProvenanceReviewRun(ref)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tbundleID = run.BundleID\n\t}\n\tbundle, err := s.LoadReviewBundle(bundleID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tctx, err := s.ReviewDraftContextFor(bundle)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\treturn s.CheckReviewDraftIn(ctx, output, now), nil\n}\n\n// CheckReviewDraftIn judges output against ctx.\nfunc (s Store) CheckReviewDraftIn(ctx ReviewDraftContext, output string, now time.Time) []string {\n\tvar reasons []string\n\tdraft, err := ParseReviewDraft(output)\n\tswitch {\n\tcase err != nil:\n\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the conclusion cannot be read: \"+err.Error())\n\tcase draft == nil:\n\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the final message carries no pose-draft block\")\n\t}\n\tif err == nil {\n\t\tround := ReviewRound{Number: ctx.Round, Open: ctx.Open}\n\t\tif problems := ValidateRoundDraft(round, output); len(problems) > 0 {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the draft does not account for its round: \"+strings.Join(problems, \"; \"))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif draft != nil && reviewDecisionApproves(draft.Decision) {\n\t\tbundle := ctx.Bundle\n\t\trun := ReviewRun{RunID: \"draft-check\", BundleID: bundle.BundleID, Kind: ReviewBriefKindReview}\n\t\tatt := reviewAttestationFromDraft(run, bundle, *draft, \"agent:draft-check/unknown\")\n\t\tcompleted, err := completeReviewAttestation(bundle, att, now)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the attestation preflight refuses it: \"+strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n\t\t} else if blockers := s.attestationContentBlockers(bundle, completed, false); len(blockers) > 0 {\n\t\t\treasons = append(reasons, \"the attestation preflight refuses it: \"+strings.Join(uniqueSorted(blockers), \"; \"))\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn reasons\n}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\nindex f76b164e..6f563a15 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\n@@ -65,6 +65,23 @@ func TestReviewDraftCheckMatchesTheConclusionStep(t *testing.T) {\n \tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", \"--draft\", draftPath); code != 0 {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the run's context refused a good draft: %d %s\", code, out)\n \t}\n+\t// Naming the run's own bundle uses the context too, where the sealed\n+\t// checkout holds no bundle file (review round 2, N5).\n+\tempty := t.TempDir()\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, empty, \"review\", \"draft-check\", bundleID, \"--draft\", draftPath); code != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"naming the run's bundle ignored the context: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, empty, \"review\", \"draft-check\", \"rvb-ffffffffffffffff\", \"--draft\", draftPath); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"this run's draft context holds bundle \"+bundleID) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"another bundle was not refused with the context named: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n+\t// A draft past the limit is refused, never judged by its prefix (N4).\n+\thuge := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"huge.txt\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(huge, append(good, make([]byte, 4<<20)...), 0o600); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"review\", \"draft-check\", \"--draft\", huge); code == 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"larger than\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"an oversized draft was judged: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t}\n \t// From standard input, as a read-only sandbox can only offer it.\n \tt.Setenv(posemodel.ReviewDraftContextEnv, \"\")\n \tstdin, _ := os.Open(badPath)\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc '\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" context --task spec:pose-review-readiness-before-seal --json; \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" suggest review --path pose-mcp; cat .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md; git diff 5c35b3a8..2bd80b69 --stat'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc '\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" context --task spec:pose-review-readiness-before-seal --json; \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" suggest review --path pose-mcp; cat .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md; git diff 5c35b3a8..2bd80b69 --stat'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"selected_project_id\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n  \"selected_revision\": \"2bd80b6903c2a7b23c1f12a6be6bb283aa0ed8e7\",\n  \"task_ref\": \"xref:proj.pose-dist/spec:pose-review-readiness-before-seal\",\n  \"authority\": {\n    \"project_id\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n    \"kind\": \"spec\",\n    \"slug\": \"pose-review-readiness-before-seal\"\n  },\n  \"coordinator_relation\": \"same-project-authority\",\n  \"task_resolution\": {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"project_id\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n      \"kind\": \"spec\",\n      \"slug\": \"pose-review-readiness-before-seal\"\n    },\n    \"resolved\": true,\n    \"resolution_state\": \"resolved\",\n    \"status\": \"in-progress\",\n    \"source_revision\": \"2bd80b6903c2a7b23c1f12a6be6bb283aa0ed8e7\",\n    \"source_digest\": \"0d976d12852296baa58ae3aa4367fb3cec2dd8c4390d88ba45a5df48b1223f7a\"\n  },\n  \"authority_revision\": \"2bd80b6903c2a7b23c1f12a6be6bb283aa0ed8e7\",\n  \"supported_contracts\": [\n    \"qualified-artifact-refs@1\",\n    \"spec-authority-transfer@1\",\n    \"federated-roadmap-acceptance@1\"\n  ],\n  \"context_revision\": \"43008253366c58377272031b33352ea6fe48f0a59a68c65c9f71d159ba00385c\"\n}\n# POSE trail — review\n\nAvaliação técnica de PR/diff: escopo, contratos, segurança, validação.\n- Path:      pose-mcp → domain: backend-go (repo-map)\n- Workflow:  .pose/workflows/review.md\n- Skill:     pose-review\n- Rules:     .pose/rules/security.md, .pose/rules/documentation-style.md, .pose/rules/backend-go.md\n- Spec:      false\n- ADR:       false\n- Knowledge: consume=true, produce=handoff (quando aceitar risco residual ou condicionar merge)\n- Validation: exigir evidência de pose validate do implementador\n---\nslug: pose-review-readiness-before-seal\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-23\ncompleted_at:\nsupersedes:\ndepends_on: \nremediates:\npriority: 1\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: feature\nsurface: standard\ndelivers: capability:review-readiness-before-seal\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-readiness-before-seal\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nRefuse at seal, and let the reviewer check inside its run, every condition the conclusion preflight and `pose close` would otherwise refuse after a full review round.\n\n### Business value\nClosing `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks` took 23 review rounds. About seven were lost to conditions known before the reviewer started: a missing delivery declaration that `close` refused only after approval, a decision with no requirement basis, a finding id with a round prefix, `prior_findings` naming findings no concluded round holds open, criterion evidence outside the criterion's component, and a note file over 16 KiB. Each cost a seal, a delegated run and about 40 minutes.\n\n### Constraints\nThe checks reuse the existing preflight and closeout predicates; no rule is duplicated. A seal refusal names the rule and the fix. Nothing weakens a gate: what is refused later is refused earlier, never accepted.\n\n### Non-goals\nCapping review rounds, changing review independence, or judging the subject itself.\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: `pose review bundle --seal` shall refuse a spec scope whose attributed changes touch a delivery root without a delivery declaration, or a governed path its artifacts do not declare, with the same findings `pose close` refuses (`undeclared-delivery`, `undeclared`).\n- R2: When the plan asks for structural mappings, the seal shall refuse a spec scope with a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint, the rule the conclusion preflight applies to a mapping basis.\n- R3: A new `pose review draft-check <run|bundle> --draft <file>` shall run inside the review sandbox without writing. It reports every reason the conclusion preflight would refuse that draft: unreadable block, prefixed new finding ids, `prior_findings` outside the open findings, criterion evidence outside its component, undeclared decisions in mappings. It exits non-zero when any applies.\n- R4: The review brief shall instruct the reviewer to run `draft-check` on its draft before finishing, and list the open prior findings it must account for.\n- R5: `pose delegate` shall refuse a note file over the adapter limit with a message naming the note, its size and the limit, instead of the generic adapter-file error.\n- R6: When the instance has a conclusions issuer but the run is not concluded automatically, `pose delegate review` shall print the exact `pose review conclude <run>` command as the next step.\n\n### Non-functional\nExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n\n### Security\nNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n\n### Compatibility\nRecords and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n`pose-mcp` (CLI and engine), the manual and its embedded copy.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n- created: .pose/adr/2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal.md\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_draft_check.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_preflight_tie_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/live_policy_reads_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_structure_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_seal_readiness_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_conclude.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n- modified: POSE.md\n- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:review-readiness-before-seal module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\n\n### API/contract changes\nNew command `pose review draft-check`; new environment variables `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT` and `POSE_REVIEW_CLI` set for delegated review runs; new brief template `review-brief/8`; `review bundle --seal` refuses two more conditions for new seals.\n\n### Data/storage changes\nThe dispatch writes `pose-review-draft-context.json` to the run's private temporary directory; nothing is written to the repository.\n\n### Technical risks\nA draft check that drifted from the conclusion would mislead reviewers; it calls the same functions, and a test compares its reasons with the conclusion's refusal. Residual limits L1 and L2 are stated in the ADR.\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Planning\n- [ ] Confirm the requirements against the current engine before starting.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n\n### Validation\n- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Basis: R3, R4\nThe draft check reuses the conclusion's parser, round accounting and attestation content checks, extracted as `attestationContentBlockers`, so it cannot accept what the conclusion refuses for content. It leaves out only the run's signature and identity, which do not exist before the run ends. See ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n\n### Decision D2\n- Basis: R1, R2\nThe seal applies only the readiness rules whose inputs exist before the review: the delivery and artifact declarations and the decision basis, the latter only when a required criterion asks for structural mappings. Evidence and trace gates of `pose close` stay at close. A bundle already sealed is returned without being judged again.\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n\n### Execution log\n- 2026-11-23: implemented R1–R6 with a regression test each, shown failing with its fix mutated out (seal refusal, decision basis, draft-check content, dispatch context, oversized note, conclude hint). `go test ./...` in `pose-mcp` passes.\n- 2026-11-23: review round 1 (rrn-fa6a6e8e1df0a0ba) requested changes. N1: the decision-basis refusal applied to plans with structural facts but no criterion asking for their mapping; it now requires a required `RequiresStructuralMapping` criterion. N2: `draft-check` rejected run ids; a run id now selects its bundle. N3: `live_policy_reads_test.go` was not declared; it is, and the seal now also refuses the `undeclared` artifact finding, which the round showed is known before the review too. The reviewer could not run `draft-check` because its shell resolved the installed `pose`; the dispatch now sets `POSE_REVIEW_CLI` to the dispatching engine and `review-brief/8` (not yet published) names it. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out.\n- 2026-11-23: review round 2 (rrn-9d5816c780952f13) ran `draft-check` through `POSE_REVIEW_CLI` on its own draft, which passed, and found N4 and N5; its cleanup was incomplete because a broad test was still running, so it could not be concluded. N4: a draft over 4 MiB was judged by its prefix; drafts over the limit are now refused from a file or standard input. N5: naming the run's own bundle inside the sealed checkout ignored the dispatch context; the context now serves the run's bundle whether it is named or not, and another reference names the context's bundle when it cannot be read. Both fixes have tests that fail with them mutated out.\n\n\n### Results summary\nThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes. The canonical validation result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry` after the implementation commit.\n\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestSealRefusesAnUndeclaredDelivery\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestSealReadinessRefusesADecisionWithoutBasis\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewDraftCheckMatchesTheConclusionStep\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestTheCurrentBriefAsksForTheDraftCheck\n- R5 [satisfied] test:TestDelegateNamesTheNoteLimitAndTheConclusionStep\n- R6 [satisfied] test:TestDelegateNamesTheNoteLimitAndTheConclusionStep\n\n\n### Known gaps\nThe draft check cannot run the signature and identity checks, which need the finished run; the conclusion step still runs them.\n\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\nThe seal of a new spec bundle refuses an undeclared delivery or artifact and, when the plan asks for structural mappings, a decision basis that reaches no requirement. `pose review draft-check` reports what the conclusion step would refuse, inside the run, through a context the dispatch writes. The brief `review-brief/8` asks for it. `pose delegate` names an oversized note and the conclude command of a run nothing concluded.\n\n\n### Files and modules changed\n`pose-mcp` (CLI and engine), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies, the ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n\n\n### Validation executed\n`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n\n\n### Residual risks\nL1 and L2 in the ADR: the draft check judges against the dispatch's context, and the seal reads the committed index.\n\n\n### Follow-ups\nNone.\n\n\n# ADR: Check review readiness before the seal and inside the run\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted on 2026-11-23 for `pose-review-readiness-before-seal`.\n\n## Context\n\nA delegated review round costs a seal, a run of about forty minutes and a conclusion. In the 23 rounds of `pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks`, about seven were lost to refusals that existed before the reviewer started: `pose close` refused an approved scope for an undeclared delivery; the conclusion preflight refused drafts for a decision with no requirement basis, prefixed finding ids, prior findings outside the open ones, and criterion evidence outside its component. The reviewer could not see those rules applied to its own draft until the run had ended.\n\n## Decision\n\nMove each check to the earliest point that has its inputs, reusing the same predicate:\n\n- The seal of a new spec bundle refuses the declaration findings the delivery index holds at error severity for the scope (`undeclared-delivery` and the artifact finding `undeclared`), which `pose close` reports. Evidence findings stay at close. When a required criterion asks for structural mappings, it also refuses a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint, the namespace the preflight checks mappings against.\n- `pose review draft-check` runs the conclusion's draft parser, the round accounting and the attestation content checks over a draft, writing nothing. The content checks are the part of the bundle-attestation validation that does not depend on the run's signature or identity, extracted as one function both paths call.\n- A sealed checkout holds neither the bundle nor the run ledger, so the dispatch writes the bundle and the round's open findings to the run's private directory and names the file in `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT`. It also names its own executable in `POSE_REVIEW_CLI`, because the reviewer's shell may resolve another installed `pose`. `--draft -` reads standard input for read-only sandboxes. A run id selects its bundle.\n- The brief of the new template `review-brief/8` asks the reviewer to run the check. Template texts are immutable, so `/7` stays for the runs briefed with it.\n\n## Consequences\n\nA scope that would fail at close now fails at seal, before any review cost. A reviewer can converge its draft inside one run. The draft check is advisory: the conclusion step stays the gate and still runs every check, including the signature and identity checks the draft check cannot run.\n\nResidual limits:\n- L1: the draft check judges against the context the dispatch wrote. A reviewer that edits that file only misleads itself, because the conclusion re-reads the sealed bundle and the ledger.\n- L2: the seal reads the delivery finding from the committed index. A stale index can miss a finding that a later `pose index` would add. `pose close` still refuses it, so the cost is a round, never a wrong closure.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- A per-instance cap on review rounds would stop the loop by approving unreviewed work.\n- Running the full `pose close` gate at seal would refuse scopes for evidence that only exists after the review.\n .pose/indexes/delivery-integrity.json              |  954 ++---\n .pose/indexes/generation.json                      |   12 +-\n .pose/indexes/spec-graph.json                      | 1170 +++---\n .pose/results/delivery-validation.json             |  948 ++---\n .pose/results/review-readiness-binding.md          |    1 +\n .../ddf2c0ff231f9dfc81765f21/000001.json           |   11 +\n .../ddf2c0ff231f9dfc81765f21/000001.result.json    |    6 +\n .pose/review-bundles/rvb-34dee7b8928be885.json     | 3770 ++++++++++++++++++++\n .pose/review-run-ledger/rrn-9d5816c780952f13.json  |    8 +\n .../review-runs/rrn-9d5816c780952f13.events.ndjson |   45 +\n .pose/review-runs/rrn-9d5816c780952f13.json        |  165 +\n .pose/review-runs/rrn-9d5816c780952f13.transcript  |   46 +\n ...2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md |    1 +\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go        |   61 +-\n pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check_test.go   |   17 +\n 15 files changed, 5661 insertions(+), 1554 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
