\t\tcase ctx != nil && (bundleID == \"\" || bundleID == ctx.Bundle.BundleID):\n    60\t\t\t// Inside a delegated review the sealed checkout holds no bundle: the\n    61\t\t\t// run's own bundle, named or not, is judged from the context the\n    62\t\t\t// dispatch wrote (review round 2, N5).\n    63\t\t\treasons = store.CheckReviewDraftIn(*ctx, string(raw), time.Now())\n    64\t\tdefault:\n    65\t\t\treasons, err = store.CheckReviewDraft(bundleID, string(raw), time.Now())\n    66\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    67\t\t\t\tmsg := strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \")\n    68\t\t\t\tif ctx != nil {\n    69\t\t\t\t\tmsg += \"; this run's draft context holds bundle \" + ctx.Bundle.BundleID + \", which is checked when it is named or no reference is given\"\n    70\t\t\t\t}\n    71\t\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Failure(\"pose review draft-check: \" + msg)\n    72\t\t\t\treturn 1\n    73\t\t\t}\n    74\t\t}\n   110\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   111\t\t\t}\n   112\t\t\tdefer f.Close()\n   113\t\t\tin = f\n   114\t\t}\n   115\t\traw, err := io.ReadAll(io.LimitReader(in, reviewDraftInputLimit+1))\n   116\t\tif err != nil {\n   117\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   118\t\t}\n   119\t\tif len(raw) > reviewDraftInputLimit {\n   120\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the draft is larger than %d bytes; a run's final message that large is not checked by a prefix\", reviewDraftInputLimit)\n   121\t\t}\n   122\t\treturn raw, nil\n   123\t}\n26:| `invented-trace-test-ref` | known-gap | A requirement trace cites a test that does not exist and `lint-spec --strict` passes (follow-up 097 of pose-abm-design-basis) | pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus |\n39:| `parity-row-cites-an-unrelated-test` | known-gap | A launcher parity row names a real but unrelated `pose delegate` command and an existing test that does not exercise the capability, and the parity check passes; the check proves existence, review of the cited tests proves coverage | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n40:| `imported-fragment-completes-a-replaced-command` | known-gap | A usage or error string assembles a removed command from a constant of another package of the module, which the active-document check reads as a gap; review of assembled messages is the defence | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n41:| `cgo-preamble-text-reaches-usage` | known-gap | Operator text written as a C string in a cgo preamble reaches a usage surface; the Go reader sees a comment, not a string | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n56:| `canned-executor-approval-proves-cognition` | delegated | A complete canned approval from a trusted local command is presented as proof of review cognition or a vendor receipt (`cli/delegated_review_capability_test.go:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityCannedApprovalDisclosesItsLimits` guards disclosure; the engine cannot detect canned judgments) | pose-delegated-review-capability |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,os\nr=json.load(open('.pose/results/delivery-validation.json'))\nprint('canonical fields:',list(r)[:18]); print({k:r[k] for k in ['mode','git_head','generated_at','engine_version'] if k in r})\nchecks=r.get('checks',[])\nprint('checks:',len(checks))\nprint('nonpassing required:',[(c.get('name'),c.get('outcome'),c.get('status')) for c in checks if c.get('severity')=='required' and c.get('outcome',c.get('status')) not in ('pass','passed')][:8])\nc=json.load(open(os.environ['POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT']))\nprint('sealed validation sample:',[(x.get('id'),x.get('outcome'),x.get('module')) for x in c['bundle']['payload']['evidence'] if x.get('id') in ('pose-mcp/go/test','pose-mcp/go/build')])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
