{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s' 'decision: approved\n\nN4 and N5 are fixed; no additional defects found. Focused tests, vet and live boundary/context probes passed. Full validation conclusions rely on the sealed canonical strict run, as allowed by the sandbox fallback.\n\nApplied the review workflow and security, backend-go and documentation-style rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nBundle: rvb-22f660b39d436e8c. Plan: sha256:94c5e8ed0db62ef3b181346f2d2219dc8a2adde13bf37aaf466973e6266f49c0.\n\n\"'```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N4\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go:115-120 reads limit+1 and refuses overflow. Live probes refused oversized stdin and /dev/stdin input, while accepting exactly 4194304 bytes; focused DraftCheck tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N5\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go:59-63 uses the dispatch context for its explicitly named bundle. Live probes accepted the same draft with an implicit reference and rvb-22f660b39d436e8c; a mismatched bundle was refused with the context'\"'\\\\''s bundle named.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the complete base-to-head implementation, spec/ADR, manuals and scaffolds, all prior fixes, declaration/basis readiness, existing-seal reuse, draft parser and round accounting, input boundaries, context selection, dispatch environment/lifecycle, note limits and conclude hints. Compared the extracted content-validation body with the base, verified existing template digests and scaffold additions, ran focused regressions/vet and live sandbox probes, and inspected sealed canonical validation. No additional defects established.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-36ac800e7cdd7060\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined D1/D2 and ADR L1/L2. Verified the context is advisory and final conclusion retains authority checks. The committed index can miss newly discovered declaration findings; close remains the final gate. These are documented design limits, not fresh evidence of readiness. Full validation conclusions use the sealed strict canonical run; focused tests, vet and sandbox probes were independently rerun.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected context publication before child start and existing dispatch cleanup/cancellation. No new goroutines or shared mutable execution state. Every command started for this review completed before the final response.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"CLI routing/help, bundle/run lookup and optional dispatch-context contracts match their documented roles. Live implicit/explicit-bundle checks agree; mismatched references fail actionably. Published brief versions retain their digests.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused regression suite passed. Live checks covered exactly-at-limit, oversized stdin/file input, implicit and explicit bundle context, and mismatch errors. Overflow is rejected instead of silently parsed as a prefix.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected CLI-to-Store routing, dispatch context/CLI environment and conclusion preflight integration. Focused dispatch and conclusion-comparison tests passed; sandbox probes used the dispatching engine.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined rule/path/remediation diagnostics, input-limit errors, context mismatch guidance, oversized-note details and conclude hints. Existing redaction remains intact.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified every preexisting template digest is unchanged and the extracted attestation-content body is textually identical to the base. Existing sealed bundles return before new readiness checks. New command/environment contracts and new-seal refusals are explicitly documented.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused readiness, draft-check, brief, sealed-gate and delegate regressions passed. Both previous failing probes now behave correctly. Shared validation extraction is unchanged; published-template and context behavior were inspected.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-36ac800e7cdd7060\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses conclusion drift by sharing parser, round accounting and content validation. D2 moves only declaration/basis checks to new seals, requires mapping owners and leaves final evidence/authority gates in place. Input overflow and explicit bundle context now preserve the intended checking boundary.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-e71849b4\\\",\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR records the R3/R4 shared validation and private context design, together with D2'\\\\''s R1/R2 timing, alternatives and L1/L2 limits.\\\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed both manuals, help, /8 instructions and prior-findings guidance. Added text matches both embedded scaffold copies exactly. Existing template digests remain unchanged; the dispatching CLI command worked in the sealed sandbox.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified actionable overflow and bundle-context errors with live commands; inspected seal remediation, named note limits and conclude commands. Both prior operational failures are resolved.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused regressions exercise R1 declaration refusals, R2 mapping applicability, R3 shared checking/context/limits, R4 brief instructions and prior findings, and R5/R6 note/conclusion guidance. Live probes independently verify the latest fixes; sealed strict validation supplies module-wide evidence.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-36ac800e7cdd7060\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Changes match the amended R1-R6 scope, declared pose-mcp capability and ADR. Previous artifact omission is corrected. The latest changes are confined to bounded draft input and dispatch-context selection with regressions.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected private 0600 context creation, bounded draft reads, existing adapter confinement and final signature/identity enforcement. Advisory context does not authorize an attestation. No new credential exposure or authority bypass found.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-36ac800e7cdd7060\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Extracting existing validation and passing a private snapshot is smaller than a second validator or premature full closeout. The latest fixes use one bounded reader and one context-selection condition. Signature/identity remain deferred. Making advisory context authoritative would invalidate the design. Nominal Basis labels or edited advisory context can satisfy form; substantive causality remains reviewer judgment and final revalidation protects authority. The adversarial corpus'\\\\''s canned-executor case documents cognition limits; no dedicated readiness corpus row exists, while focused negative tests and live overflow/context probes cover these mechanical boundaries.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict --json\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independently executed through POSE_REVIEW_CLI; result recorded after completion.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded from the sealed checkout. Inspected sealed structure:design-36ac800e7cdd7060 and mapped its governance delta.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment publication was excluded. Inspected component source and focused regressions directly.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded. Inspected CLI/dispatch/conclusion boundaries and sealed integration evidence; ran live sandbox probes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded. Direct searches found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers in the new readiness/draft-check files.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the recorded conclusion of this review; the reviewer must not record an attestation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the recorded conclusion of this review; the reviewer must not record an attestation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independently executed through POSE_REVIEW_CLI. Applied security, backend-go and documentation-style rules; consulted delivery-evidence and the review workflow.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independently executed strict surface-check through POSE_REVIEW_CLI and inspected sealed component integration evidence.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Pass cites the sealed canonical execution, not a fresh full rerun: delivery-validation.json records strict mode, 236 checks and no nonpassing required check. The read-only review independently reran focused regressions and vet as permitted by the brief'\\\\''s sandbox fallback.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Pass cites sealed pose-mcp canonical validation; full module validation was not rerun in this sandbox. Independently passed go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\\\\''DraftCheck|SealReadiness|SealRefuses|DelegateNamesTheNoteLimit|Brief|SealedGate|OnlyTheSigning'\\\\'' and go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/pose ./internal/cli.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```'\"' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
